ds and pack buffers, and staged publication and invalidation. W41 observes transient icon manifest and PNG sources, publishes complete PNGs and verifies OpenGL upload state and codec retirement. W42 joins the live creature and item cache records, item fingerprints and state, and shares each of the two preview renderers across its actual routes. W43 observes cold status publication, the three shared asset tables and the shared creature mesh uploads. W44 joins the shared item and creature texture owners and verifies alias, refusal and reload retirement. W45 observes retained rigid sources and keeps the mesh buffers alive in all queued creature and equipment mesh requests. W46 composes observed detached skeletal, glTF, item, rigid, legacy mesh and draw allocations across actual preview, world, queue, held and first-person owners. W47 joins the cold visual document and binary stages with managed source retirement and checks the accessor extents. W48 joins moved skeletal mesh assembly and its exact selected candidate requests, removes copied item JSON and small attribute arrays, and releases glTF geometry scratch earlier. W49 joins the explicit visual read buffers, the observed simultaneous stream associations and selected item/glTF resource path backings. W50 bounds explicit item traversal backing by node count and verifies deep decode and error retirement without native scene recursion. W51 bounds the static UCRT FILE slots and lowio tables and observes process handle counts. W52 bounds selected visual STL path operations and observes the real item texture directory owner. Complete remaining filesystem callers, Windows-internal file and search state, kernel handle/object memory and remaining platform accounting. Finish transient candidate ownership, remaining native stack, driver, diagnostics and old/current publication joins before the process composition. Include renderer scratch, static fallback graphics, per-actor appearance and pose, and temporary/out-of-scope visual holders in the remaining source composition. Confirm warmed legacy equipment/viewmodel and enabled foot diagnostic owner routes in a targeted native fixture. Preserve the W40 service, W41 codecs and W42 icon evidence. Include cold status catalog and visual cache construction as separate source owners. Preserve native tab and recovery behavior. Continue with other actual overlays and callbacks. Account shared renderer, shader and text roots through existing owner census. Unknown or externally-supplied objects remain open. Then complete all actual world/pool/input/OS-thread domains, escaped and detached owners, process-exit, window/capture service/GLFW and unpinned E11 construction. CRT per-thread parameter storage and per-thread data, retained loader layers, kernel handles, directory iterator opening and advance peaks, shared CRT slot and locale ownership, exception and system costs remain open. Logger cold init/rollback,historical main30344 remainder,VLOG/site/symbolizer/signal/utility roots,cleaner scans,stdio/CRT/locale/ exception/stack/TLS loader/OS/driver/GPU/total process still need explicit source/platform envelopes. No global asset/ process quota introduced. Complete original matched whole-process/RSS/high-water/frame/performance/memory/native matrix under S6.06/S6.05. S4.02 then S4.03..06/S5/S6 OPEN;23/42 unchanged;ecology S6.05 [-48,-1] data vs [-48,-4] oracle OPEN. Full S0..S6 preserved,no reduced acceptance.",
